Proves the VALUE of a compile-time constant: `bit_rt_root_host_target` returns
the BuildTarget ordinal this archive was emitted for (2 on aarch64-macos). The
evidence is the emitted immediate and its agreement with the seed's own
`hostTarget()` primitive — the whole program is one call and one print, with no
heap object whose survival could mean anything, so there is no rooting claim to
make and no loop that could honestly manufacture one.

This program's OWN code never reaches a safepoint (no loop, confirmed by
inspection), but `BIT_GC=stress` still does not report zero: 5/5 runs measured
`collections=101`, matching stress.bit's own documented scheduler-loop floor
(runtime/sched/workerrun.bit's `Worker.run`). None of those 101 fire at a
back-edge this program emitted, so they still verify nothing about this
program's rooting.
